.\" Title: vrl-cat
.\" Author: vrl contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-CAT 1 "2025" "vrl" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrl\-cat \- show VTTY text output of a command in a running instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrl
\fBcat\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the virtual terminal (VTTY) buffer of a command running inside a vrl instance. The output is plain text with ANSI escape sequences stripped, suitable for piping to \fBgrep\fR(1), \fBless\fR(1), or redirecting to a file.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrl/control\-{pid}.sock\fR and retrieves the VTTY snapshot.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrl instance (the vrl process itself, not the child command).

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
ID of the target command within the instance (omit for the first/only command).

.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of all commands in the instance and allow the user to select one or more by number (space-separated). Overrides \-c.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Print the VTTY of the only command in an instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl cat 12345\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Print a specific command by ID:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl cat 12345 \-c cmd_abc\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Interactively select commands to print:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl cat 12345 \-\-interactive\fR
  1) htop (PID 5678)
  2) vim notes.txt (PID 5679)
Select [space-separated numbers]: 1 2
.fi
.RE

.PP
Pipe output to grep:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl cat 12345 | grep "ERROR"\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, connection failed, command not found, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrl (1),
.BR vrl\-list (1),
.BR vrl\-keys (1),
.BR vrl\-spawn\-in (1)
